/-!
# The entropic-time spine is kernel-clean — an enforced build invariant

Physlib's honesty bar is that the central entropic-dynamics → quantum-mechanics → gravity chain depends only
on the three standard Lean axioms `propext`, `Classical.choice`, `Quot.sound` — *kernel-clean*, never the
compiler-trust axioms of `native_decide` (`ofReduceBool`/`ofReduceNat`/`trustCompiler`) and never an exotic
postulate. An empirical scan confirmed the curated `witnessed_by` declarations of
`Physlib.Meta.EntropicSpineZil` are kernel-clean; this module turns that scan into a
**build-enforced invariant** by running the strict
`#physlib_axiom_clean` gate (from `AxiomWhitelistCheck`, built on Lean's own `collectAxioms`) over every spine
witness plus the recovery / Born-rule capstones. If any future edit taints the spine with a non-standard
axiom, this module fails to elaborate.

The `native_decide` compiler-trust axioms remain confined to ~14 peripheral computation files, none of which
is reachable from the spine witnesses audited here. This module adds no definitions, aliases, axioms, or proof
terms; production roots do not import it.
-/

@[expose] public section

open Physlib.Meta.AxiomWhitelistCheck

namespace Physlib.Meta.SpineAxiomAudit

/-! ### One batch gate over the complete entropic spine

