The AQFT form of Landauer's principle over existing carriers: one bit at the Hawking temperature
costs a pure modular quantum, the Clausius product `β·ΔQ_bit = k_B log 2`, a QTM trace pays its
measurement count in modular quanta, `K = −log Δ` at the wedge-eigenvalue level, and the wedge
algebra and its causal complement share the full center (no totally separate algebras). -/

